# Settings keeps its live row state across pane moves: Float, Tear out (second window),
# Return to primary, Dock. The distinctive state is an unapplied edit on "Show shellbar"
# with the arrangement editor open: only a row holding a draft is offered
# "Delete (draft must be settled)" instead of "Delete", so that button in the window that
# owns the pane is the witness. (Not "Discard edit": node selectors match substrings and
# the theme row's "Discard edits and reload" contains it.) Run headed with a fresh
# TURNSTONE_ROOT. Free window-position moves have no scenario verb; this is the
# pane-custody move only. An emptied torn-out window stays open after Return (windows
# stays 2); the Dock step below runs in the primary window.
settle 20
key escape
resize 1180 950
open mere://settings-reactive
settle 10
act id:pane:settings
settle 5
assert pane turnstone.settings
click surface:settings .toggle
settle 3
click surface:settings role:button Edit arrangement
settle 3
assert windows == 1
assert node role:button Delete (draft must be settled)

act Float pane
settle 8
assert windows == 1
assert pane turnstone.settings
assert node role:button Delete (draft must be settled)

act Tear out pane
settle 10
assert windows == 2
assert lens-pane turnstone.settings
assert no-pane turnstone.settings
assert node window:1 role:button Delete (draft must be settled)
assert node window:1 role:switch Toggle

act Return pane to primary
settle 10
assert pane turnstone.settings
assert no-lens-pane turnstone.settings
assert node role:button Delete (draft must be settled)

act Dock pane
settle 8
assert pane turnstone.settings
assert node role:button Delete (draft must be settled)
assert node role:switch Toggle
log Settings draft survived float, tear out, return and dock
